  "title": "Placement: what JS already does in your head",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "md": "## No fox yet\n\nEight short questions about what JavaScript actually does. Wrong answers do not lock you out — they mark which later lessons to take slowly.\n\nPick the result you expect the language to produce, not the result you wish it produced. Later, the same ideas show up as a fox on a field and as a signal board on a page."
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "id": "typeof-null",
      "promptMd": "`typeof null` is…",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "null",
          "md": "`\"null\"`"
        },
        {
          "id": "object",
          "md": "`\"object\"`",
          "misconceptionId": "null-is-object-ok"
        },
        {
          "id": "undefined",
          "md": "`\"undefined\"`"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "object",
      "explainMd": "`typeof null` is the string `\"object\"`. That is a lie the language kept. Later you will treat `null` as its own empty value, not as an object you can poke.",
      "diagnostic": true,
      "skillIds": [
        "js.values"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "id": "strict-eq",
      "promptMd": "`0 === \"\"` is…",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "true",
          "md": "true — they feel empty",
          "misconceptionId": "double-equals-is-fine"
        },
        {
          "id": "false",
          "md": "false — different kinds"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "false",
      "diagnostic": true,
      "skillIds": [
        "js.values"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "id": "truthy-zero",
      "promptMd": "`if (0) { \"go\" } else { \"stop\" }` yields…",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "go",
          "md": "`go`"
        },
        {
          "id": "stop",
          "md": "`stop`"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "stop",
      "diagnostic": true,
      "skillIds": [
        "js.flow"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "id": "closure-sniff",
      "promptMd": "`function make() { let n = 0; return () => ++n } const a = make(); a(); a();` — `a()` now returns…",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "1",
          "md": "`1` — each call starts over",
          "misconceptionId": "closure-copies-value"
        },
        {
          "id": "3",
          "md": "`3` — `n` is still the same box"
        },
        {
          "id": "2",
          "md": "`2`"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "3",
      "diagnostic": true,
      "skillIds": [
        "js.closures"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "id": "map-vs-mutate",
      "promptMd": "`const xs = [1]; const ys = xs.map(n => n + 1)` — `xs[0]` is…",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "2",
          "md": "`2` — map rewrote the list",
          "misconceptionId": "map-mutates"
        },
        {
          "id": "1",
          "md": "`1` — map returned a new list"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "1",
      "diagnostic": true,
      "skillIds": [
        "js.arrays"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "id": "promise-vs-cb",
      "promptMd": "A `Promise` that is waiting to finish is in which state?",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "pending",
          "md": "pending"
        },
        {
          "id": "callback",
          "md": "callback — that is the same thing"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "pending",
      "diagnostic": true,
      "skillIds": [
        "js.async"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "id": "this-sniff",
      "promptMd": "A plain `function greet() { return this }` called as `greet()` in sloppy Node often sees `this` as…",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "undefined-strict",
          "md": "always `undefined`"
        },
        {
          "id": "globalish",
          "md": "the global object (unless `\"use strict\"`)"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "globalish",
      "diagnostic": true,
      "skillIds": [
        "js.this"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "id": "dom-sniff",
      "promptMd": "`document.querySelector(\"#beacon\")` returns…",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "string",
          "md": "the HTML as a string"
        },
        {
          "id": "node",
          "md": "one element node, or `null` if missing"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "node",
      "diagnostic": true,
      "skillIds": [
        "js.dom"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "description": "A short quiz about what you already expect JavaScript to do. Wrong answers do not lock you out."
